{"script":"export const meta = {
  name: 'kvflash-moe-preflight',
  description: 'Verify load-bearing assumptions of the KVFlash-MoE 128K plan against current HEAD before any implementation',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Verify', detail: 'independent read-only checks of each plan assumption' },
    { title: 'Synthesize', detail: 'go/no-go on starting Phase 1 + corrected line numbers' },
  ],
}

const FINDING = {
  type: 'object',
  additionalProperties: false,
  required: ['claim', 'verdict', 'evidence', 'corrected'],
  properties: {
    claim: { type: 'string', description: 'the plan assumption being checked' },
    verdict: { type: 'string', enum: ['CONFIRMED', 'DRIFTED', 'FALSE', 'MISSING', 'UNCLEAR'] },
    evidence: { type: 'string', description: 'file:line + the actual code/text found, terse' },
    corrected: { type: 'string', description: 'corrected line numbers / facts if DRIFTED, else "n/a"' },
  },
}

const CWD = '/home/peppi/Dev/lucebox-hub'

const CHECKS = [
  {
    label: 'moe-hard-errors',
    prompt: `In ${CWD}, the plan claims qwen35moe hard-errors when prompt > pool at server/src/qwen35moe/qwen35moe_backend.cpp lines 777-785 (generate path) and 1401-1409 (restore path). Read those regions (and search the file for error strings about pool/kvflash/prompt-too-large). Verify both hard-errors exist, quote them, and give exact current line numbers. Also confirm the file's total line count.`,
  },
  {
    label: 'hybrid-forward-batch',
    prompt: `In ${CWD}, the plan claims Qwen35MoeBackend::hybrid_forward_batch() at server/src/qwen35moe/qwen35moe_backend.cpp:1578 is a complete pooled+slot-masked+slot-mapped MoE forward, doing alloc_span+slot_of (~1608), kv_write_rows (~1614-1654), slot-space mask (~1678-1708), in-place DeltaNet threading, hot/cold/spark MoE routing. Read the function. Confirm it exists, its real start line, and which of those sub-features are actually present. Quote the alloc_span/slot_of/kv_write_rows/mask lines.`,
  },
  {
    label: 'dense-do-prefill',
    prompt: `In ${CWD}, the plan uses Qwen35Backend::do_prefill() at server/src/qwen35/qwen35_backend.cpp:954-1208 as the template, with the kvf_paged branch defined at lines 976-977 (kvf_paged = kvflash_active() && prompt_len > kvflash_tokens_ - chunk_tokens()). Read it. Confirm the function range, the exact kvf_paged definition line + expression, the chunk loop, slot_for usage, zero_free_blocks() + mask-epoch bump post-prefill. Give corrected line numbers.`,
  },
  {
    label: 'pager-header',
    prompt: `In ${CWD}, read server/src/common/kvflash_pager.h fully. The plan claims: NO serialize()/deserialize() today; file ends ~385 lines; slot_for at ~165; ensure_free_block at ~322 (sink+tail protection then score_hook/LRU); reselect at ~286 (tau-step); protection predicate referencing lines ~329-332 and ~293-294; min_pool_tokens at ~75-77; NO pinning API. Verify each: confirm serialize/deserialize truly absent, confirm pinning absent, and give corrected line numbers for slot_for, ensure_free_block, reselect, min_pool_tokens, and the two protection-predicate sites.`,
  },
  {
    label: 'snapshot-structs',
    prompt: `In ${CWD}: (1) read the PrefixSnapshot struct in server/src/qwen35/internal.h and list its current fields (plan wants to add kvflash_blob + is_pooled). (2) Read snapshot_target_cache / restore_target_cache in server/src/qwen35/qwen35_target_graph.cpp around lines 1385-1599 — confirm they exist, their real line ranges, and whether a skip_kv flag already exists. (3) Read server/src/qwen35/qwen35_backend.cpp around 413-423 for the snapshot_save pooled guard (plan says it returns false when pooled) and quote it.`,
  },
  {
    label: 'commit-53f63767',
    prompt: `In ${CWD}, run: git log --oneline | head -40, and git show --stat 53f63767 (the plan's snapshot-restore fix). Confirm the commit is present in the current tree (or a rebased equivalent), report what files it touched and a one-line summary. Also report: current branch (git branch --show-current), git status --short summary (how dirty), and the server/deps/llama.cpp submodule pinned commit (git -C server/deps/llama.cpp rev-parse HEAD) — plan expects 9cd9e1ed.`,
  },
  {
    label: 'build-feasibility',
    prompt: `In ${CWD}, assess build feasibility for C++-only edits to server/src/qwen35moe and server/src/common. Check: does a build/ dir with prebuilt CUDA artifacts exist (look for build/dflash_server or build/bin, .o/.a CUDA objects, and a recent dflash_server binary)? Is build/compile_commands.json present and does it contain entries for qwen35moe_backend.cpp and kvflash_pager (header-only, check a TU that includes it)? Report the cmake build target name for the server, the binary path, and whether the memory-noted per-TU recompile+relink workaround (compile changed .cpp with /usr/bin/c++ using compile_commands flags, relink against prebuilt CUDA artifacts) is viable here. Do NOT start a build.`,
  },
  {
    label: 'bench-harness',
    prompt: `In ${CWD}, confirm the benches the plan's gates depend on exist and are runnable. Check: harness/clients/run_claude_code.sh (agentic W3); optimizations/pflash/tests/niah_gen.py (W1 drop-variant base) and bench_niah_cpp.py (grader); the flock path /tmp/dflash_gpu.lock convention (grep harness for flock usage). For each, report exists/missing + a one-line note on its interface (key env vars like MAX_CTX, how a server binary is pointed at via DFLASH_SERVER_BIN). List anything the plan references that is missing.`,
  },
]

phase('Verify')
const findings = await parallel(CHECKS.map(c => () =>
  agent(c.prompt, { label: c.label, phase: 'Verify', schema: { type: 'object', additionalProperties: false, required: ['label', 'findings'], properties: { label: { type: 'string' }, findings: { type: 'array', items: FINDING } } } })
))

const clean = findings.filter(Boolean)
return { checks: clean }
"}

