std::vector<ggml_tensor *> attn_k_, attn_v_;
std::vector<ChunkState> chunks_;
std::vector<int> free_blocks_;
std::vector<uint8_t> zero_buf_;
KvFlashStats stats_;
size_t k_seg_bytes_ = 0, v_seg_bytes_ = 0, chunk_bytes_ = 0;
int n_blocks_ = 0, n_head_kv_ = 0, cur_chunk_ = 0;
uint64_t clock_ = 0;
uint64_t epoch_ = 0;
```

**`ChunkState` inner struct (lines 315-320):**
```cpp
struct ChunkState {
    int      block = -1;       // pool block index, -1 = not resident
    bool     on_host = false;  // backing store holds valid bytes
    uint64_t last_use = 0;
    std::vector<uint8_t> host_data;
};
```

Field-by-field inventory:

| Field | Type | Role |
|-------|------|------|
| `cfg_` | `KvFlashConfig` | chunk_tokens, pool_tokens, sink_chunks, tail_window_chunks |
| `attn_k_` | `vector<ggml_tensor*>` | Per-full-attention-layer K cache tensors (pool-sized), shape `[head_dim, pool_tokens, n_head_kv]` |
| `attn_v_` | `vector<ggml_tensor*>` | Same for V |
| `chunks_` | `vector<ChunkState>` | Per-logical-chunk state: block assignment, host residency, host bytes, LRU clock |
| `free_blocks_` | `vector<int>` | Pool block indices currently unoccupied (stack; back = next to allocate) |
| `zero_buf_` | `vector<uint8_t>` | Scratch zeros for zeroing freed blocks; max(k_seg_bytes_, v_seg_bytes_) bytes |
| `stats_` | `KvFlashStats` | Counters: page_outs, page_ins, host_bytes, moved_bytes |
| `k_seg_bytes_` | `size_t` | Bytes for one K head-segment: `chunk_tokens * K0->nb[1]` |
| `v_seg_bytes_` | `size_t` | Same for V: `chunk_tokens * V0->nb[1]` |
| `chunk_bytes_` | `size_t` | Total host_data size per chunk: `(k_seg_bytes_ + v_seg_bytes_) * n_head_kv_ * n_layers` |
| `n_blocks_` | `int` | `pool_tokens / chunk_tokens` — total physical blocks |
| `n_head_kv_` | `int` | KV head count (from `K0->ne[2]`) |
| `cur_chunk_` | `int` | Append-head chunk index — used to define the protected tail window |
| `clock_` | `uint64_t` | LRU tick; incremented on every `slot_for` hit |
| `epoch_` | `uint64_t` | Residency-change counter; callers use to invalidate cached masks |

**What serialize must capture:** `chunks_` (all block assignments + on_host flags + host_data payloads), `cur_chunk_`, and the resident KV bytes from the GPU pool tensors. `free_blocks_`, `clock_`, `epoch_`, `stats_` are reconstructable and need not be serialized (though clock/epoch should be reset on deserialize).

---

